# The WireGuard component comes from the ESP Component Registry and has
# no Kconfig of its own. Its header reads CONFIG_WIREGUARD_MAX_SRC_IPS to
# size the per-peer allowed-address array; the default is 1, which the
# device's own tunnel address already occupies. This firmware adds
# 0.0.0.0/0 as a second entry, so the array must have at least two slots.
config WIREGUARD_MAX_SRC_IPS
    int
    default 4
    help
        Maximum number of allowed source/destination addresses per
        WireGuard peer. One entry is taken by the device's own tunnel
        address; the firmware adds 0.0.0.0/0, which needs another.
